    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a6">

                <pb facs="0709" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg623"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garcia to Mr.
                            De Long.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation del Peru</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Yedo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1873-07-22"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22, 1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your excellency’s note No. 56, dated 20th instant, addressed in
                    duplicate to the gaimusho and to this legation, in which you inclose copies of
                    published notice of sale and of inventory of the bark Maria Luz.</p>
                <p>Giving you my sincere thanks for your note and its in closures, I beg your
                    excellency to accept the renewed expressions of my high consideration and
                    regard,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>AURELIO GA <hi rendition="#small-caps">y</hi>
                            GARCIA.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
